#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:5
msgid "Assembly"
msgstr "装配体"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:7
msgid ""
"**Assembly** is the assembly instruction book: a page per step, drawn, to "
"read here or save. It is for an assembly, and it is what :doc:`Build "
"</digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build>` lists the steps of -- the "
"same steps, in the same order, as a document."
msgstr ""
"**Assembly** 就是那本装配说明书：每个步骤一页，都画出来，可以在这里阅读，也可以保存下来。它针对装配体，而它正是 :doc:`Build "
"</digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_build>` 所列出步骤的那个东西 -- "
"同样的步骤、同样的顺序，只是作为一份文档。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:12
msgid ""
"The book is written from the assembly itself. Each link of the ASSY file "
"says what it is joined to and how -- pushed, snapped or screwed in -- so the"
" step that adds it can be written out for a person to follow, with the two "
"parts drawn pulled apart by the ``exploded:`` gap of the connection. Nothing"
" about the book is declared separately from the assembly, which is why it "
"cannot fall out of step with it."
msgstr ""
"这本说明书是从装配体自身写出来的。ASSY 文件的每一条链接都说明它与什么接合以及如何接合 -- 压入、卡入还是拧入 -- "
"所以添加它的那一步就能写出来供人照着做，其中那两个零件按该连接的 ``exploded:`` "
"间隙拉开来绘制。关于这本说明书的任何内容都不是与装配体分开声明的，这也正是它不可能与装配体步调不一致的原因。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:20
msgid "In the UI"
msgstr "在界面中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:22
msgid ""
"The document, as **PDF** or **HTML**, with **Recursive** and **Build parts**"
" -- which are ``pc instructions -r -b`` -- and **Save…**."
msgstr ""
"那份文档，形式为 **PDF** 或 **HTML**，并带有 **Recursive** 和 **Build parts** -- 也就是 ``pc "
"instructions -r -b`` -- 以及 **Save…** 。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:25
msgid ""
"The Manufacturing group's Assembly tab: the assembly instruction book, page "
"by page"
msgstr "Manufacturing 组的 Assembly 标签页：装配说明书，一页一页地看"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:30
msgid ""
"Manufacturing is for a part or an assembly; for a scene, a sketch or an "
"interface the whole group is disabled, and this tab is for an assembly "
"alone."
msgstr "Manufacturing 针对零件或装配体；而对场景、草图或接口，整个这一组都是禁用的，至于这个标签页则只针对装配体。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:34
msgid "On the command line"
msgstr "在命令行中"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:43
msgid ""
"``-r`` puts in the steps of every sub-assembly that is built, each just "
"before the step that adds it, and ``-b`` how to make every part that is "
"built, each just before the step that first needs it. Both read the "
":doc:`Build vs Buy </digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>` choices "
"made on this machine."
msgstr ""
"``-r`` 会把每一个自制子装配体的步骤都插进来，各自紧排在添加它的那一步之前；而 ``-b`` "
"会插入每一个自制零件的制造方法，各自紧排在第一个需要它的步骤之前。两者都会读取本机上所做的 :doc:`Build vs Buy "
"</digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_bvb>` 选择。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:50
msgid "How the steps are decided"
msgstr "这些步骤是如何决定的"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:52
msgid ""
"See :ref:`how an assembly is manufactured <assembly-manufacturing>` and "
":doc:`/assy` for what each ``connect:`` says about the joining -- the "
"mating, the ``how:``, the torque and the thread -- and "
":doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing` for the ``connect`` check, which is"
" what reports a step the declaration says nothing about."
msgstr ""
"每个 ``connect:`` 关于接合所说的内容 -- 那个配合、那个 ``how:`` 、扭矩和螺纹 -- 参见 :ref:`装配体是如何制造出来的"
" <assembly-manufacturing>` 和 :doc:`/assy` ；而 ``connect`` 检查参见 "
":doc:`/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing` ，它正是报告某一步在声明中什么都没说的那项检查。"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/manufacturing_assembly.rst:59
msgid "Agent skills"
msgstr "智能体技能"

